{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505516-ravnos-the-most-powerful-antediluvian","id":1505516,"title":"Ravnos the most powerful antediluvian","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-16T16:58:29-07:00","id":1505516,"title":"Ravnos the most powerful antediluvian","content":"Can we all agree that Ravnos is the most powerful antediluvian and faked his own death? Well maybe not the latter (but possibly). I am willing to accept he was in wight form when he woke up and didn't use his hax illusion powers to try to fool the world but come on, he has to have been the most powerful of them all!<br /> <br /> We are talking about someone who basically had access to the reality stone. Anything he thinks about becomes reality. It's the most powerful disclipline that you can have at level 10. You don't need any other discipline. He could think all the other level 10 disciplines in existence if he wanted or create his own disciplines on the fly (reminds of Caine in that department).What could possibly match that?<br /> <br /> I am interested to hear genuine arguments about which antediluvian you think is more powerful. But don't give a cop out answer like: they are all as powerful as the storyteller wants lol<br /> <br /> Give me hard cold facts that proves the contrary or accept Ravnos as the biggest badass of them all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T18:52:34-07:00","id":1505522,"title":"","content":"[Tzimisci] and Gangrel are the two surviving Antediluvians in final storyline in the Gehenna book. It's hard to beat [Tzimisci] simultaneously becoming every living being on the entire planet. Other than Gangrel becoming the planet...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T22:16:09-07:00","id":1505527,"title":"","content":"In his rage, Ravnos used Chimerstry 10 to turn all of reality into a role playing game, and that is what happened.<br /> <br /> Seriously though, I don\u2019t recognize the Week of Nightmares in any chronicles that I run. In my opinion, the Antediluvians don\u2019t die until Gehenna, so if I were forced to use the Week of Nightmares, I would rule that Ravnos faked his death. Antediluvians\u2019 power is so great that it defies comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T02:01:04-07:00","id":1505532,"title":"","content":"Canon says he's dead ergo hes dead. Probably was the most powerful because chim 10 is true magic but no Paradox most powerful isn't infinite. Either Cappadocius ot tzmisce are/were probably 2nd.<br /> <br /> <br /> Its also more interesting plot wise that some of the 3rd gen are dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-17-2023, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T03:59:17-07:00","id":1505533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505516-ravnos-the-most-powerful-antediluvian#post1505516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are talking about someone who basically had access to the reality stone. Anything he thinks about becomes reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emperor Joker, The Scarlet Witch, Proteus, The Shaper of Worlds, Mad Jim Jaspers... all reality shapers, and what have in common?<br /> They were all defeated<br /> Chimestry is a delicate discipline<br /> Lv 7.\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b <b>Suspension of Disbelief</b>: Make an illusion seem completely real or what is real seem unbelievable\u200b<br /> Lv 8. <b>Fantasy World</b>: Place a target in an illusionary world in their mind<br /> Lv 9. <b>Mayaparisatya</b>: Temporarily make an illusion completely real or alter a person or 